fact WorkItem(id: "WI-557", description: some(value: "Scope the WI-539 call-site value-precondition requires-check to op-body context (it currently leaks into rule-body dot-dispatch). The WI-539 requires-check lives in check_apply_iter, which is ALSO reached by the rule-body dot-dispatch pass (dispatch_rule_body_dots -> dispatch_dots_in_occ -> type_check_node -> check_apply_iter) with a STRUCTURALLY EMPTY Gamma. A value precondition over a rule-body variable then floats (definite_only) -> spurious TypeError::UnsatisfiedPrecondition, which is currently SWALLOWED by the pre-existing Err(_) wildcard in dispatch_dots_in_occ (typing.rs). Doubly latent today (no value-precondition requires exist in stdlib; the error is swallowed) but conceptually wrong: a rule body is SLD/relational, not imperative-with-Gamma, so the op-body Hoare requires-check does not apply there. Two candidate approaches (from user): (a) handle the value-precondition discharge in req_insertion::run -- the post-typecheck requires-threading pass that already walks OP BODIES (kb.op_bodies) and add/removes requires, so it is naturally scoped to op-body context and never sees rule bodies; CAVEAT: Gamma is built during the typing pass (check_apply_iter / the iterative typer), so a req_insertion-time check needs Gamma available or rebuilt (the inline check has it for free) -- weigh persisting/recomputing Gamma vs the inline approach. (b) simpler: in the rule-body dot-dispatch context just MARK the precondition succeeded (gate the check off) -- needs an op-body-vs-rule-body discriminator threaded to check_apply_iter (e.g. a flag on TypingEnv set by dispatch_rule_body_dots' empty env, or gate on an enclosing-op marker). Deferred from WI-539 (Part 1) because a careless inline gate risks a SILENT OVER-SKIP that the contract-less test suite cannot catch (no value-precondition requires to regress on). Acceptance: a test where a value-precondition op is invoked in a RULE body raises NO spurious UnsatisfiedPrecondition, while op-body requires-checking (the WI-539 tests) is unchanged."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-539"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-25T10:33:30Z"))

